<h1>Challenge a judgment</h1>
<p class="emst-lede">If a task, indicator, crosswalk or label looks wrong, tell us. AI agents drafted these records and no practitioner has reviewed them yet, so corrections from people who do the work are how the taxonomy improves.</p>
<ol class="usa-process-list">
  <li class="usa-process-list__item"><p class="usa-process-list__heading">Copy the record ID</p><p>Every task, competency and drawer shows an ID such as <code>emst:water/CMP-H9HHYEF</code>. Copy it, with the release ID <code>{{ emst.release.id }}</code>.</p></li>
  <li class="usa-process-list__item"><p class="usa-process-list__heading">Say what is wrong and what would be right</p><p>Describe the work as you see it. Please do not include names, contact details or anything about identifiable people.</p></li>
  <li class="usa-process-list__item"><p class="usa-process-list__heading">Open an issue on the project's GitHub Issues page</p><p>Go to <a class="emst-url" href="https://github.com/jrwashebek/Enviroskillstaxonomy/issues" rel="noreferrer">github.com/jrwashebek/Enviroskillstaxonomy/issues</a> and open a new issue with the record ID, the release ID and what you would change. The same page takes questions about the pilot. GitHub is a third-party service with its own terms, and you need a GitHub account to open an issue; agency staff should check their agency's policy first. This explorer itself sends nothing and has no feedback form.</p></li>
</ol>
